              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261017004555.2890038-1-joannelkoong@gmail.com/",
              "subject": "[PATCH v2] mm: unqueue deferred split folios outside the lruvec lock",
              "date": "2026-10-17T00:48:12Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch modifies the Linux kernel to unqueue deferred split folios from a list outside of the lruvec lock, which is held during critical sections that run with IRQs disabled and are highly contended. The existing callers of folio_unqueue_deferred_split() without holding the lruvec lock serve as precedent for this change. A new function, folio_batch_unqueue_deferred_split(), is introduced to unqueue each batch of zero-refcount folios from the deferred split list after the lruvec lock is released and before mem_cgroup_uncharge_folios(). This modification aims to shorten the critical sections under the lruvec lock and reduce contention. Testing with a microbenchmark shows that this patch reduces runtime costs and contention on the lruvec lock.",
