          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch addresses long stalls in kernfs due to allocation of inodes and dentries while holding the kernfs_rwsem lock, which can lead to memory reclaim delays and OOM killer activations. The patch allocates inodes outside the lock and frees them if unused, similar to previous commits for other use cases. This change reduces wait times in various scenarios, including cgroupfs operations, and improves overall system performance.",
